IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lhl-dates`
IMPORT `lhl-rules`

-- Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (Vic) -- the questions of the PROVIDER.
--
-- SEAT: the person who provides, or wants to provide, labour hire services: a sole trader, a partner in a business run
-- jointly, or the officer answering for a company; the applicant for a licence and the holder of one. "Do I provide labour
-- hire services?", "Is my licence in force?", "Am I breaking s 13?", "May I advertise?", "May I apply yet?", "What must go
-- with my application?", "Must the Authority grant it?", "How long can my licence last?", "By when must I report, pay,
-- respond, notify?", "Must I show my licence to this person?", "Can I refuse to answer?", "Can I go to VCAT?", "What is the
-- most I can be ordered to pay, and by when can I be pursued?". The Labour Hire Licensing Authority, the Commissioner,
-- inspectors, VCAT and the courts get no seat: their satisfaction, beliefs and decisions are asked as facts. The host's
-- questions are in lhl-seat-host.l4, the worker's in lhl-seat-worker.l4.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of lhl-rules.l4. The
-- duties with deadlines (ss 34, 43, 44) are DEONTIC rules run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Labour Hire
-- Licensing Act 2018, Version No. 009 (1 October 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Labour hire licensing in Victoria: the provider's questions`

§§ `Do I need a licence (ss 7 to 11, 13, 14)`

@export Do I provide labour hire services under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 7 to 10)? You do if, in a business, you supply workers you pay to work for others; or, in a recruitment or placement business, you place workers with others who pay them and also arrange their accommodation; or, in a contractor management business, you recruit independent contractors for others and manage their contracts. The regulations can add or exclude cases.
GIVEN `my business` IS A `Kind of business` @desc The business you conduct: a business of providing recruitment or placement services; a business of providing contractor management services; another business; or no business
      `the arrangement is mainly` IS A `Character of the arrangement` @desc What your arrangement with the other business (the host) is, wholly or principally: the supply of labour; recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for the host; or something else
      `how the individuals are engaged` IS A `How the individuals are engaged` @desc How the individuals who do the work are engaged: a provider (you or another) supplies them to others to perform work and must pay them for it; a provider recruits or places them with others who must pay them; a provider recruits them as independent contractors for others and manages their contract performance; or none of these
      `I arrange their accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you procure or provide accommodation for the individuals for some or all of the time they do the work
      `the regulations take it to be labour hire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Labour Hire Licensing Regulations prescribe circumstances that take what you do to be providing labour hire services (answer no if unsure)
      `the regulations exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude you, the services you provide, or the individuals you supply or place, from the Act (answer no if unsure)
      `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude the individuals (or the services they provide) from being workers under the Act (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do I provide labour hire services` MEANS
    `ss 7 to 10 -- provides labour hire services` (`The arrangement` WITH
        `the kind of business` IS `my business`
        `the character` IS `the arrangement is mainly`
        `the engagement` IS `how the individuals are engaged`
        `accommodation is procured or provided for the individuals` IS `I arrange their accommodation`
        `the regulations take it to be labour hire services` IS `the regulations take it to be labour hire`
        `the regulations exclude the provider, services or individuals` IS `the regulations exclude it`
        `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers` IS `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers`)

@export Is my labour hire licence in force on a given day under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 26, 28, 39, 40)? A licence is in force from the day it starts until its expiry date, unless suspended or cancelled; an application to renew made in the prescribed period keeps it in force until the renewal is decided or withdrawn.
GIVEN `I hold a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold (or held) a licence under the Act
      `the day it came into force` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence came into force (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
      `its expiry date` IS A DATE @desc The expiry date shown on your licence
      `it was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority cancelled your licence (at your request or otherwise)
      `the day the cancellation took effect` IS A DATE @desc If it was cancelled, the day the cancellation took effect (any day otherwise)
      `it is suspended on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence is suspended on the day you are asking about
      `I applied to renew it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to renew your licence
      `the day I applied to renew` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you made the renewal application (any day otherwise)
      `I applied in the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the renewal application was made in the period the regulations prescribe for renewals
      `the renewal has been decided or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the renewal application has been decided (renewed or refused) or withdrawn
      `the day it was decided or withdrawn` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was decided or withdrawn (any day otherwise)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my licence in force` MEANS
    `the licence is in force on` (`The licence` WITH
        `there is a licence` IS `I hold a licence`
        `the day it came into force` IS `the day it came into force`
        `the expiry date` IS `its expiry date`
        `it has been cancelled` IS `it was cancelled`
        `the day the cancellation took effect` IS `the day the cancellation took effect`
        `it is suspended on the day` IS `it is suspended on that day`
        `a renewal application was made` IS `I applied to renew it`
        `the day the renewal application was made` IS `the day I applied to renew`
        `it was made in the prescribed period` IS `I applied in the prescribed period`
        `the renewal application has been decided or withdrawn` IS `the renewal has been decided or withdrawn`
        `the day it was decided or withdrawn` IS `the day it was decided or withdrawn`) `the day asked about`

@export Am I breaking the rule against providing labour hire services without a licence, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 13)? A person must not provide labour hire services unless they hold a licence that is in force; the maximum civil penalty is 800 penalty units for an individual and 3200 for a company. Answer the labour hire questions first: this takes their answer and whether your licence is in force.
GIVEN `I provide labour hire services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide labour hire services (the answer to the question on whether you provide labour hire services)
      `my licence is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a licence that is in force on the day (the answer to the question on whether your licence is in force; no if you hold none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I providing labour hire services without a licence` MEANS
    `s 13 -- providing labour hire services without a licence` `I provide labour hire services` (JUST `my licence is in force`)

@export Am I forbidden to advertise, or hold myself out as offering, labour hire services, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 14)? You may not unless you hold a licence that is in force; the maximum civil penalty is 200 penalty units for an individual and 800 for a company.
GIVEN `my licence is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a licence that is in force on the day (no if you hold none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I forbidden to advertise labour hire services` MEANS
    `s 14 -- advertising labour hire services is forbidden` (JUST `my licence is in force`)

§§ `Applying for a licence (ss 3, 17, 18, 23, 24, 29, 32)`

@export Am I barred from applying for a labour hire licence, or for renewal, on a given day under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 18)? You may not apply within 2 years after a labour hire licence of yours (in Victoria or elsewhere) was cancelled, unless at your own request or in prescribed circumstances, or within 3 months after an application of yours was refused or the refusal upheld.
GIVEN `the day I want to apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you want to make the application
      `a licence of mine was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a labour hire licence you held under this Act or another labour hire law (in any State or Territory) was cancelled
      `the day it was cancelled` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was cancelled (any day otherwise)
      `it was cancelled at my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was cancelled on your own initiative
      `the cancellation was in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cancellation happened in circumstances the regulations prescribe (for example a transfer of the business); answer no if unsure
      `an application of mine was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier application of yours for a labour hire licence (under any labour hire law) was refused, or its refusal upheld on review or appeal
      `the day of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was refused, or the refusal was upheld (any day otherwise)
      `the refusal was in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the refusal was in circumstances the regulations prescribe; answer no if unsure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I barred from applying` MEANS
    `s 18 -- I must not apply` (`my history` `a licence of mine was cancelled` `the day it was cancelled` `it was cancelled at my request` `the cancellation was in prescribed circumstances` `an application of mine was refused` `the day of the refusal` `the refusal was in prescribed circumstances`) `the day I want to apply`

@export From what day may I apply for a labour hire licence, or for renewal, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 18)? The second anniversary of a cancellation that counts, or 3 months after a refusal that counts; if neither bars you, the day you want to apply.
GIVEN `the day I want to apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you want to make the application
      `a licence of mine was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a labour hire licence you held under this Act or another labour hire law was cancelled
      `the day it was cancelled` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was cancelled (any day otherwise)
      `it was cancelled at my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was cancelled on your own initiative
      `the cancellation was in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cancellation happened in circumstances the regulations prescribe; answer no if unsure
      `an application of mine was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier application of yours for a labour hire licence was refused, or its refusal upheld on review or appeal
      `the day of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was refused, or the refusal was upheld (any day otherwise)
      `the refusal was in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the refusal was in circumstances the regulations prescribe; answer no if unsure
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day may I apply` MEANS
    `s 18 -- the first day I may apply` (`my history` `a licence of mine was cancelled` `the day it was cancelled` `it was cancelled at my request` `the cancellation was in prescribed circumstances` `an application of mine was refused` `the day of the refusal` `the refusal was in prescribed circumstances`) `the day I want to apply`

@export Which tier is my labour hire business, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 3)? Tier 1: turnover of no more than $2 000 000 a year; tier 2: $2 000 001 to $10 000 000; tier 3: more than $10 000 000. Turnover is total ordinary income from running the business, over the 4 quarters before the information is due, or projected for the first 4 quarters of a new business. The regulations may prescribe other amounts.
GIVEN `the turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc The business's turnover in dollars: for the 4 quarters before the day the turnover information is due, or, if the business did not operate in those quarters, its projected turnover for its first 4 quarters
GIVETH A `Tier`
`Which tier is my business` MEANS `s 3 -- the tier of the business` `the turnover`

@export What declarations, consents and acknowledgements must go with my application for a labour hire licence, or for renewal, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 17, 23, 28, 29)? The list depends on whether you already run a labour hire business and whether you arrange accommodation or transport for workers.
GIVEN `the kind of application` IS A `Kind of application` @desc Whether it is an application for a licence (s 17) or an application to renew a licence (s 28)
      `I already conduct a labour hire business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you apply, you are already conducting a business that provides labour hire services
      `we arrange accommodation for workers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, an officer or a nominated officer procures, or intends to procure, accommodation for workers in connection with the labour hire services
      `we arrange transport for workers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, an officer or a nominated officer procures, or intends to procure, transport for workers in connection with the labour hire services
GIVETH A LIST OF `What must go with it`
`What must go with my application` MEANS
    `ss 17, 23, 28, 29 -- what must go with the application` `the kind of application` `I already conduct a labour hire business` `we arrange accommodation for workers` `we arrange transport for workers`

@export Must the Labour Hire Licensing Authority grant (or renew) my licence under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 24, 29, 32(4))? It must if the application is complete, you were not barred from applying, the fee is paid and it is satisfied that everyone involved is fit and proper, complies with the laws, and that you are financially viable; otherwise it may still grant if satisfied that is appropriate, and must otherwise refuse. If someone objected, it must first take the objection and your response into account.
GIVEN `it includes the required information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application includes all the information required (s 17(2), (3) for a new licence; the prescribed information for a renewal)
      `it has the required declarations and consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is accompanied by all the required declarations, consents and acknowledgements
      `I was not barred from applying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were free to apply under s 18 (see the question on being barred from applying)
      `I paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the prescribed application fee (if any) was paid
      `the Authority is satisfied everyone is fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority is satisfied that you, your officers or decision makers and your nominated officers are each a fit and proper person
      `the Authority is satisfied everyone complies with the laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority is satisfied each of them has complied, is complying and will continue to comply with the Act, the regulations and the laws in s 23(1A) (tax, super, safety, workers' compensation, workplace, migration and others)
      `further information was given to its satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any further information, documents, consents, statutory declarations or access the Authority required were given to its satisfaction (yes if none was required)
      `the Authority is satisfied I am financially viable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority is satisfied you can pay your debts as and when they fall due
      `the Authority is satisfied it is appropriate anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not every condition is met, whether the Authority is satisfied it is appropriate in all the circumstances to grant or renew the licence anyway
      `someone objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an interested person lodged an objection to your application
      `the objection has been taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the Authority has taken into account the objection and your response (if any)
GIVETH A `What the Authority must do`
`Must the Authority grant my licence` MEANS
    `ss 24, 29, 32(4) -- what the Authority must do` (`The application as decided` WITH
        `it includes the required information` IS `it includes the required information`
        `it has the required declarations, consents and acknowledgements` IS `it has the required declarations and consents`
        `the applicant was not barred by s 18` IS `I was not barred from applying`
        `the prescribed fee was paid` IS `I paid the prescribed fee`
        `satisfied each relevant person is fit and proper` IS `the Authority is satisfied everyone is fit and proper`
        `satisfied each relevant person complies` IS `the Authority is satisfied everyone complies with the laws`
        `further information required was given to its satisfaction` IS `further information was given to its satisfaction`
        `satisfied the applicant is financially viable` IS `the Authority is satisfied I am financially viable`
        `satisfied it is appropriate in all the circumstances` IS `the Authority is satisfied it is appropriate anyway`
        `an objection was made` IS `someone objected`
        `the objection and response have been taken into account` IS `the objection has been taken into account`)

@export By when may I respond to an objection to my labour hire licence application under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 32(3))? The Authority must allow you 14 days from the day it forwards the objection to you.
GIVEN `the day it was forwarded` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority forwarded the notice of objection to you
GIVETH A DATE
`By when may I respond to the objection` MEANS `ss 32(3), 42(2) -- the last day to respond` `the day it was forwarded`

§§ `Holding a licence (ss 26, 29, 34, 35, 42, 43, 44)`

@export What is the last day my labour hire licence (or renewed licence) can be in force under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 26, 29(7))? A licence lasts at most 3 years from the day it came into force; a renewed licence at most 3 years from the old licence's expiry date.
GIVEN `the day counted from` IS A DATE @desc For a first licence, the day it came into force; for a renewed licence, the expiry date of the licence it renews
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day my licence can be in force` MEANS `ss 26, 29(7) -- the last day the licence can be in force` `the day counted from`

@export By when must I give the Labour Hire Licensing Authority my annual information for a reporting period under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 34)? Within 28 days of the start of each 12-month reporting period, counted from the day the licence first came into force.
GIVEN `the day my licence first came into force` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence first came into force
      `the reporting period` IS A NUMBER @desc Which reporting period: 1 for the first 12 months, 2 for the next, and so on
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give my annual information` MEANS
    `s 34(3) -- the last day for the annual information` `the day my licence first came into force` `the reporting period`

@export Did I give, or can I still give in time, my annual information for a reporting period under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 34)? It is a condition of the licence to give it within 28 days of the start of the reporting period; breaching a condition carries a civil penalty of up to 200 penalty units for an individual and 800 for a company (s 36).
GIVEN `the day my licence first came into force` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence first came into force
      `the reporting period` IS A NUMBER @desc Which reporting period: 1 for the first 12 months, 2 for the next, and so on
      `I have given it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Authority the information for that period
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you gave it (any day otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Did I give my annual information in time` MEANS
    `s 34 -- what became of the annual information` `the day my licence first came into force` `the reporting period` `I have given it` `the day I gave it` `today`

@export When does my next annual labour hire licence fee fall due under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 35(1))? On the day the licence was specified to come into force (or to be renewed) and on each anniversary of it. The amount is set by the regulations.
GIVEN `the day specified` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence was specified to come into force, or to be renewed
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A DATE
`When is my next annual fee due` MEANS `s 35(1) -- the next day the annual fee falls due` `the day specified` `today`

@export From what day may I pay my next annual labour hire licence fee early under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 35(2))? At any time in the 6 weeks before it falls due.
GIVEN `the day specified` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence was specified to come into force, or to be renewed
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day may I pay my annual fee` MEANS
    `s 35(2) -- the first day the fee may be paid early` (`s 35(1) -- the next day the annual fee falls due` `the day specified` `today`)

@export By when may I respond to the Authority's notice that it proposes to vary or cancel my labour hire licence (show cause notice) under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 42)? Within 14 days after the notice is given; the Authority must consider your response before deciding.
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the show cause notice was given to you
GIVETH A DATE
`By when may I respond to the show cause notice` MEANS `ss 32(3), 42(2) -- the last day to respond` `the day the notice was given`

@export Did I notify the Labour Hire Licensing Authority of a change in time, or can I still, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 43, 44)? A licence holder must notify any change in the information given to the Authority, and any prescribed change, within 30 days of the change. The maximum civil penalty is 40 penalty units for an individual and 160 for a company (s 43), or 800 and 3200 for a prescribed change (s 44).
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE @desc The day the change happened
      `I have notified it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the Authority of the change
      `the day I notified it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you notified it (any day otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Did I notify the change in time` MEANS
    `ss 43, 44 -- what became of the notice of the change` `the day of the change` `I have notified it` `the day I notified it` `today`

§§ `Inspections (ss 46, 67, 67A, 91)`

@export Must I show my labour hire licence to the person asking, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 46)? A licence holder must produce it for inspection when asked by an inspector, a provider, a worker for a provider, a host, a police officer or a prescribed person. Not doing so is an offence: up to 12 penalty units for an individual, 60 for a company.
GIVEN `who asked` IS A `Who asked` @desc Who asked to see the licence: an inspector; a provider; a worker for a provider; a host; a police officer; a person prescribed by the regulations; someone else; or nobody has asked
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I show my licence` MEANS `s 46 -- the licence must be produced` `who asked`

@export Until what day must I keep my labour hire business documents available for inspection after my licence ends, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 67(2))? For 6 years after the licence ceases to be in force (if it is not renewed).
GIVEN `the day my licence ceased` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence ceased to be in force
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when must I keep my documents available` MEANS `s 67(2) -- the last day the documents must be available` `the day my licence ceased`

@export Does an inspector's notice to produce my labour hire business documents give me the time the Act requires, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 67(4))? The notice must give at least 14 days from its date.
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the inspector's notice
      `the day it says to comply by` IS A DATE @desc The day by which the notice says you must comply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does the notice give me enough time` MEANS `s 67(4) -- the notice gives at least 14 days` `the date of the notice` `the day it says to comply by`

@export Can I refuse to give information to an inspector because it might incriminate me, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 91)? For an individual, yes for information and other things required under Part 5, but not for producing a document.
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a natural person (not a company)
      `what I am required to do` IS A `What I am required to do` @desc What you are required to do: give information or answer questions; produce a document; or do another thing under Part 5
      `it would tend to incriminate me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether doing it would tend to incriminate you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I refuse because it would incriminate me` MEANS
    `s 91 -- self-incrimination is a reasonable excuse` `I am an individual` `what I am required to do` `it would tend to incriminate me`

§§ `Review and penalties (ss 93, 94, 97, 98, 102, 105)`

@export Can I apply to VCAT for review of a decision of the Labour Hire Licensing Authority under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 102)? The applicant (or an objector) may seek review of decisions to grant, refuse, renew or refuse to renew a licence; the holder may seek review of conditions, notices to comply, variations, suspensions and cancellations.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision: to grant a licence; to refuse to grant a licence; to renew a licence; to refuse to renew a licence; to impose a condition on a licence; to issue a notice to comply; to vary a licence; to refuse your application to vary a licence; to suspend a licence; to cancel a licence; or another decision
      `my part` IS A `My part in it` @desc Your part in it: the applicant for the licence or its renewal; the holder of the licence; an interested person who objected to the application; or someone else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply to VCAT` MEANS `s 102 -- I may apply to VCAT for review` `the decision` `my part`

@export By when must I apply to VCAT for review of a Labour Hire Licensing Authority decision under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 102)? Within 28 days of being notified of the decision.
GIVEN `the day I was notified` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the decision
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to VCAT` MEANS `s 102 -- the last day to apply to VCAT` `the day I was notified`

@export What is the most I can be ordered to pay, in penalty units, for a contravention or offence under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 46 to 88, 94)? For example 800 penalty units (3200 for a company) for providing labour hire services without a licence. The dollar value of a penalty unit is set each year under the Monetary Units Act 2004. Assaulting or threatening an inspector (s 88(2)) can also bring up to 2 years' imprisonment for an individual.
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision contravened` @desc The provision: s 13 providing labour hire services without a licence; s 14 advertising without a licence; s 15(1) entering into an arrangement with an unlicensed provider; s 16(2) an avoidance arrangement; s 16(3) not reporting one; s 36 a licence condition; s 37(3) a notice to comply; s 43 not notifying changes; s 44(1) prescribed changes; s 45 nominated officers; s 67(1) or (2) documents; s 86(1) threats; s 86(2) dismissal or detriment; or the offences in ss 46, 67(5), 67A(5), 74(2), 79(2), 84(2), 85(2), 87, 88(1), 88(2)
      `I am a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate (answer no for an individual)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be ordered to pay` MEANS `the maximum penalty units for` `the provision` `I am a company`

@export Can a court still order me to pay a civil (pecuniary) penalty for a contravention of Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018, and which court (ss 93, 97, 98)? The Authority must apply within 6 years of the contravention; there is no pecuniary penalty after a conviction for substantially the same conduct, and the civil case waits while criminal proceedings go on. Larger penalties go to the Supreme Court only.
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision contravened` @desc The provision said to be contravened (see the question on the most you can be ordered to pay for the list)
      `I am a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate (answer no for an individual)
      `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day of the contravention
      `the day the Authority applies` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority applied (or would apply) to the court
      `I was convicted for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of an offence constituted by conduct substantially the same as the contravention
      `criminal proceedings are under way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether criminal proceedings for an offence constituted by substantially the same conduct have been started against you and are not finished
GIVETH A `Whether a pecuniary penalty can be ordered`
`Can I be ordered to pay a civil penalty` MEANS
    `Part 6 -- whether a pecuniary penalty can be ordered` `the provision` `I am a company` `the day of the contravention` `the day the Authority applies` `I was convicted for the same conduct` `criminal proceedings are under way`

@export Until what day can I be prosecuted for an offence under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 105)? Proceedings may be commenced within 6 years after the date of the alleged offence.
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence is alleged to have been committed
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when can I be prosecuted` MEANS `s 105 -- the last day to commence a prosecution` `the day of the offence`

§§ `Helpers (not questions)`

-- Builds the s 18 history record from the seat's plain inputs.
GIVEN `cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN, `cancelled on` IS A DATE, `at my request` IS A BOOLEAN, `prescribed cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused on` IS A DATE, `prescribed refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The history`
`my history` `cancelled` `cancelled on` `at my request` `prescribed cancellation` `refused` `refused on` `prescribed refusal` MEANS
    `The history` WITH
        `a licence of mine was cancelled` IS `cancelled`
        `the day it was cancelled` IS `cancelled on`
        `it was cancelled on my initiative` IS `at my request`
        `the cancellation was in prescribed circumstances` IS `prescribed cancellation`
        `a prior application of mine was refused` IS `refused`
        `the day it was refused or the refusal upheld` IS `refused on`
        `the refusal was in prescribed circumstances` IS `prescribed refusal`
